L000257	{\it Structure of the sign of the equal-time spin-spin correlation function}---
L000258	Here we further analyze the equal-time spin-spin correlation function, focusing on its sign pattern and ignoring its amplitude, plotted in Fig.~\ref{fig:ftsign}(a) and (b) for the LE and HE states, respectively. While the short-ranged correlations marked by the shaded region are identical for the two states, the longer-ranged correlations are significantly different. The LE state mostly follows a three-sublattice pattern, similar to the 120$^\circ$ state, while the HE state exhibits a striped pattern.
